# Server/Client Boundaries

- Default to Server Components; push `use client` to leaves.
- Never pass functions/components from server to client props.
- Props across the boundary must be serializable.
- Client components own dynamic imports.

```tsx
// bad: server passes function prop
<ClientComponent ServerChild={ServerChild} />

// good: client owns lazy import
const HeavyComponent = lazy(() => import('./HeavyComponent'));
```

## Theme styling (`sx` and CSS variables)

- `sx` must be plain serializable objects; use CSS variables (`--dg-palette-*`, `--dg-shadow-*`, or collage tokens) and static spacing.

```tsx
// good: CSS vars + plain object
<Box sx={{ color: 'var(--dg-palette-text-primary)', padding: '8px' }} />
```

## Avoid `component={Function}`

- Do not pass a function/component to `Box` or `Typography`'s `component` prop across a server-client boundary; use wrapper components (`Link`, `PageTransitionLink`) or HTML tag strings instead.

```tsx
// good
<Link href="/music">Music</Link>
<Typography component="h1">Heading</Typography>
```
